/*
  core/masks/naive_verify.spthy -- f_H for the NEW Naive mask, VERIFY_KEY action.
  (Plan §3: the Clueless user with no mental model of the abstract check -- PGP key metaphor.)

  Naive ACCEPTS the fingerprint of ANY kind, including a 'tampered' one -- a Norman MISTAKE
  (confident wrong action from a wrong mental model), NOT a slip. RespMask(P,'Naive') is gated
  by the current-mask restrictions: Naive must be the current mask (set by sigma6 Abstraction).
*/

rule Verify_Naive_mistake:
    [ !VerifyReq(P, vid, kind) ]
  --[ Verify(P, vid, 'Naive'), RespMask(P,'Naive'), Mistake(P, vid), Accept(P, vid), Answered(vid) ]->
    [ !KeyChecked(P, vid) ]
